From: Artem Pelenitsyn <a.pelenitsyn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:54:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Pass the version macros of cabal_macros.h to mhs

GHC includes cabal_macros.h with -optP-include. mhs passes on to cpphs only
the -D and -I options it is given, so give it the macros of the header one
by one, as MicroCabal does: generateCabalMacrosOptions renders the same data
as generateCabalMacrosHeader as -D options, VERSION_<pkg> and
MIN_VERSION_<pkg>(major1,major2,minor) for the package and its dependencies,
the TOOL_ variants for the configured programs, and the CURRENT_ constants,
the first definition of a macro winning as in the header. The autogen
directory of the component is on the include path of cpphs too, so a module
that includes cabal_macros.h itself finds it.

Many packages choose code on these macros, transformers for instance its
Semigroup instances, and without them took the branch for an ancient base.

The test of mhs moves to PackageTests/MHS/Build, and PackageTests/MHS/Macros
checks the macros; it is skipped unless mhs and its cpphs are installed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
